APX.bg = {"country":{"name":"Bulgaria","tagline":"Dionysus's homeland, the Cabernet that taught Britain to drink red, and native grapes such as Mavrud and Broadleaf Melnik finding their voice again.","classification":"Under EU rules Bulgaria has 52 PDOs (*защитено наименование за произход*, ZNP) and two PGIs (*защитено географско указание*): Тракийска низина (Thracian Lowlands) and Дунавска равнина (Danube Plain). The PDOs, registered in 2007 (Bolyarovo in 2009), are mostly named after a town and its surrounding municipalities, inherited from the socialist-era Controliran (DGO/DGOC) system; most serious producers prefer the two PGIs, which are flexible and widely recognised. The Executive Agency for Vine and Wine (IAVV) supervises the system. Traditional terms include *резерва* (reserve), *специална резерва* and *премиум*."},"regions":[{"name":"Danubian Plain","slug":"danubian-plain","tagline":"North Bulgaria between the Danube and the Balkan range: Gamza, Cabernet and the old export wineries.","ids":["bg-lom","bg-lovech","bg-lozitsa","bg-lyaskovets","bg-montana","bg-novo-selo","bg-pavlikeni","bg-pleven","bg-ruse","bg-suhindol","bg-svishtov","bg-vidin","bg-vratsa"]},{"name":"Black Sea","slug":"black-sea","tagline":"The north-east and the coast: Dimyat, Riesling and crisp whites near Varna and Pomorie.","ids":["bg-chernomorski-rayon","bg-dragoevo","bg-evksinograd","bg-han-krum","bg-novi-pazar","bg-pomorie","bg-shumen","bg-targovishte","bg-varbitsa","bg-varna","bg-veliki-preslav","bg-yuzhno-chernomorie"]},{"name":"Rose Valley","slug":"rose-valley","tagline":"The Sub-Balkan valley of roses beneath the Balkan range: Red Misket and cool whites.","ids":["bg-hisarya","bg-karlovo","bg-karnobat","bg-shivachevo","bg-slavyantsi","bg-sliven","bg-sungurlare"]},{"name":"Thracian Lowlands","slug":"thracian-lowlands","tagline":"The Maritsa basin and Sakar hills: Mavrud, Rubin and Bulgaria's richest reds.","ids":["bg-asenovgrad","bg-bolyarovo","bg-brestnik","bg-haskovo","bg-ivaylovgrad","bg-lyubimets","bg-nova-zagora","bg-oryahovitsa","bg-pazardzhik","bg-perushtitsa","bg-plovdiv","bg-sakar","bg-septemvri","bg-stambolovo","bg-stara-zagora","bg-yambol"]},{"name":"Struma Valley","slug":"struma-valley","tagline":"The warm south-west by Greece: Broadleaf Melnik, sandstone pyramids and Bulgaria's smallest town.","ids":["bg-dolinata-na-struma","bg-harsovo","bg-melnik","bg-sandanski"]}],"items":{"bg-asenovgrad":{"name":"Asenovgrad","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Mavrud, Rubin, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Asenovgrad, at the edge of the Rhodopes south-east of Plovdiv, is the traditional heartland of Mavrud, the late-ripening, thick-skinned native red that makes dark, tannic wines with blackberry, mulberry and spice. The PDO covers Asenovgrad, Parvomai and Sadovo municipalities. Legend ties the grape's name to a young man of Khan Krum's time whose wine-fuelled courage saved the vineyards.","producers":["Zagreus","Todoroff"],"nerd_note":"Mavrud vines are often trained low and need a long, warm autumn; the best old vines sit on the alluvial terraces of the Chaya river below the Rhodope foothills.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-bolyarovo":{"name":"Bolyarovo","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2009","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Syrah","summary":"Bolyarovo, near the Turkish border south-east of Yambol, was registered in 2009 as the last of Bulgaria's PDOs. Its municipality is a remote, hot strip of vineyard on the eastern Sakar plateau.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-brestnik":{"name":"Brestnik","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Mavrud, Rubin, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Brestnik, a village in the Rodopi municipality just south of Plovdiv, has its own PDO for reds from Mavrud, Rubin, Cabernet and Merlot grown on the first Rhodope foothills. Its slopes rise just above the Maritsa plain, where the alluvial soils give way to the stonier ground that Mavrud prefers.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-chernomorski-rayon":{"name":"Chernomorski Rayon","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Dimyat, Riesling, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Traminer, Muscat Ottonel","summary":"Chernomorski Rayon ('Black Sea Region') is the broadest Bulgarian PDO, covering 47 municipalities of north-east Bulgaria from Dobrich and Varna to Shumen, Razgrad and Silistra. It is the umbrella for the region's whites.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-dolinata-na-struma":{"name":"Dolinata na Struma","cat":"PDO","region":"Struma Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiroka Melnishka Loza, Melnik 55, Keratsuda, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Syrah","summary":"Dolinata na Struma ('Struma Valley') is the broad PDO covering 22 municipalities along the Struma from Pernik and Kyustendil south to Petrich and Sandanski, including Blagoevgrad and Kresna. It frames all the south-west's wine styles, from Broadleaf Melnik and Melnik 55 to Cabernet, Merlot and the rare Keratsuda white of Kresna.","producers":["Logodaj","Orbelus","Damianitza"],"rslug":"struma-valley"},"bg-dragoevo":{"name":"Dragoevo","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Riesling, Aligoté","summary":"Dragoevo, a village near Veliki Preslav, has a small white-wine PDO in the Novi Pazar and Veliki Preslav municipalities. Its vineyards lie on the same limestone plateau as Preslav's, below the 10th-century capital's ruins. Today the name is rarely seen on labels.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-evksinograd":{"name":"Evksinograd","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Riesling, Chardonnay, Dimyat","summary":"Evksinograd (Euxinograd) is the former royal summer palace on the coast just north of Varna, built in the 1880s for Prince Alexander of Battenberg. Its estate vineyards give their name to a tiny PDO.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-han-krum":{"name":"Han Krum","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Traminer, Riesling, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"Han Krum, a village named after the 9th-century khan of the Mavrud legend, has a large winery long known for white wines, especially Chardonnay and Traminer. Its PDO covers three municipalities around Shumen and Preslav.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-harsovo":{"name":"Harsovo","cat":"PDO","region":"Struma Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiroka Melnishka Loza, Melnik 55, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Harsovo, a village in the Sandanski municipality near Melnik, gives its name to a small PDO in the heart of Broadleaf Melnik country. Villa Melnik's estate is nearby. Like the rest of the Struma valley it enjoys the warm air that funnels north from the Aegean.","producers":["Villa Melnik"],"rslug":"struma-valley"},"bg-haskovo":{"name":"Haskovo","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon, Syrah, Mavrud, Rubin","summary":"The Haskovo PDO spans six municipalities in the south-east, from the Rhodope foothills to the Sakar hills. Castra Rubra, named after a nearby Roman fort, is the region's flagship estate.","producers":["Castra Rubra"],"rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-hisarya":{"name":"Hisarya","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Rubin, Misket","summary":"Hisarya is a Roman spa town with intact 4th-century walls. Its municipality includes Starosel, where the Thracian temple complex of Chetinyova Mogila stands near a modern winery and spa built around the wine-and-Thracians theme.","producers":["Starosel"],"rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-ivaylovgrad":{"name":"Ivaylovgrad","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Mavrud, Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Ivaylovgrad is in the far south-east near the Greek border, in the warm eastern Rhodopes, close to the Roman villa of Armira with its mosaics. Its PDO is for reds, especially Mavrud and Merlot.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-karlovo":{"name":"Karlovo","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white","red"],"grapes":"Misket Cherven, Muscat Ottonel, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Karlovo, at the western end of the Rose Valley beneath the Balkan range, covers five municipalities. The area is known for Misket and Red Misket whites. Karlovo is also where the Rose Valley's oil-rose harvest begins each May, and the valley's sheltered position between two mountain ranges keeps its whites aromatic and fresh.","rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-karnobat":{"name":"Karnobat","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Misket Cherven, Muscat Ottonel, Rkatsiteli, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Karnobat, inland from Burgas, covers the Karnobat and Straldzha municipalities. It makes whites and reds, and is historically a big brandy and wine centre. Its position between the Black Sea and the eastern Balkan range gives a mild climate suited to both aromatic whites and Bordeaux reds.","rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-lom":{"name":"Lom","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Gamza, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Lom, a Danube port in the north-west, has a single-municipality PDO for reds and whites from loess terraces above the river. Lom was one of Bulgaria's main Danube ports, and its river terraces are warm and well drained.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-lovech":{"name":"Lovech","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Gamza","summary":"Lovech, at the foot of the central Balkan range, has a small single-municipality PDO for reds and whites from cooler, hillier ground. The town sits on the Osam river where the plain meets the Balkan foothills, so its vineyards are a little cooler and later-ripening than those of the Danube lowlands.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-lozitsa":{"name":"Lozitsa","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Gamza","summary":"Lozitsa, whose name means 'little vine', is a village in the Nikopol municipality on the Danube. It has a small PDO for wines from the loess bluffs. Nikopol was an important Danube fortress town, and the north-facing river terraces give fresh, medium-bodied wines.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-lyaskovets":{"name":"Lyaskovets","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white","red","sparkling"],"grapes":"Aligoté, Chardonnay, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Lyaskovets, near Veliko Tarnovo, has a long winemaking tradition and a winery known for sparkling and still wines; the PDO covers its municipality. Lyaskovets is a few kilometres from Veliko Tarnovo, capital of the Second Bulgarian Empire, and its winery has a long tradition of traditional-method sparkling wine.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-lyubimets":{"name":"Lyubimets","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon, Syrah, Mavrud","summary":"Lyubimets covers the eastern Sakar hills and the lower Maritsa (Harmanli, Lyubimets, Stambolovo, Svilengrad and Topolovgrad municipalities). It is warm Merlot and Cabernet country, and the former state cellar at Lyubimets was a major exporter.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-melnik":{"name":"Melnik","cat":"PDO","region":"Struma Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red"],"grapes":"Shiroka Melnishka Loza, Ranna Melnishka Loza (Melnik 55), Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"The Melnik PDO covers the Petrich municipality around the tiny town of Melnik, Bulgaria's smallest with about 400 inhabitants, set among the sandstone and conglomerate 'earth pyramids' that rise up to 100 m above the Struma valley. Its grape is Shiroka Melnishka Loza (Broadleaf Melnik), a late-ripening red with small, dark berries that ripens in October and makes spicy, tobacco-scented, oak-loving wines; Melnik 55, its early-ripening offspring bred at Sandanski in 1963, is softer and riper. Melnik wine has been recorded since at least 1346, was shipped to Venice and beyond from merchants' rock-cut cellars such as the Kordopulov House (1754), and is said to have been Winston Churchill's favourite Bulgarian wine.","terroir":"Sandy and sandstone soils at the foot of the Pirin; hot, dry sub-Mediterranean climate funnelled up the Struma valley.","producers":["Villa Melnik","Zlaten Rozhen","Mitko Manolev","Sintica"],"nerd_note":"Shiroka Melnishka Loza is a parent of Ranna Melnishka Loza (Melnik 55), whose other parent DNA testing identified as the French Valdiguié.","rslug":"struma-valley"},"bg-montana":{"name":"Montana","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Gamza, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Montana covers nine municipalities in the north-west between the Balkan range and the Danube; Gamza and Cabernet are the main reds. The area's limestone and loess soils and continental climate give medium-bodied reds, and Gamza here is light and peppery.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-nova-zagora":{"name":"Nova Zagora","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pinot Noir, Mavrud, Chardonnay","summary":"Nova Zagora covers six municipalities east of Stara Zagora, including Chirpan and Sliven's southern edge, and is the only Bulgarian PDO registered for quality sparkling wine as well as still wine. Edoardo Miroglio's estate at Elenovo and Midalidare near Chirpan are the leading producers.","producers":["Edoardo Miroglio","Midalidare"],"rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-novi-pazar":{"name":"Novi Pazar","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Riesling, Muscat Ottonel","summary":"Novi Pazar, east of Shumen on the north-eastern plateau, has a small PDO for whites (registered with the Veliki Preslav municipality). It shares the limestone-rich plateau and cool, breezy conditions that made the Shumen-Preslav area Bulgaria's white-wine heartland under socialism.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-novo-selo":{"name":"Novo Selo","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Gamza, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Novo Selo, a Danube village in the Vidin province, is the classic home of Gamza (Kadarka), which makes light, peppery, red-fruited wines here; the PDO covers its municipality. The Danube moderates temperatures, letting the late-ripening, thin-skinned grape reach full ripeness without losing its freshness.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-oryahovitsa":{"name":"Oryahovitsa","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Rubin, Mavrud, Syrah","summary":"Oryahovitsa, a village near Stara Zagora on the southern slopes of the Sredna Gora, is home to the Oriachovitza winery, founded in 1936, which became famous in the 1980s for Cabernet-Merlot blends exported to the UK. Its own vineyards sit at 170 to 260 m.","producers":["Oriachovitza"],"rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-pavlikeni":{"name":"Pavlikeni","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Gamza","summary":"Pavlikeni, in the central north, has a single-municipality PDO. Its winery was another of the export-era Cabernet and Merlot producers. Its loess-covered hills between the Danube and the Balkan range give medium-bodied, fruity reds, and Gamza also grows here.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-pazardzhik":{"name":"Pazardzhik","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon, Syrah, Petit Verdot, Mavrud","summary":"The Pazardzhik PDO lies in the upper Maritsa valley west of Plovdiv (registered with the Septemvri municipality). The area's best-known modern estate is Bessa Valley, founded in 2001 by Count Stephan von Neipperg of Château Canon-la-Gaffelière and Karl-Heinz Hauptmann, which makes Merlot-led reds.","producers":["Bessa Valley"],"rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-perushtitsa":{"name":"Perushtitsa","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Mavrud, Rubin, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Perushtitsa, south-west of Plovdiv at the foot of the Rhodopes, is the second classic home of Mavrud; its PDO covers part of the Rodopi municipality. The town is also a national shrine for its role in the April Uprising of 1876.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-pleven":{"name":"Pleven","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Rubin, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Gamza","summary":"Pleven is home to Bulgaria's Institute of Viticulture and Enology, where Rubin was bred in 1944, and a wine museum in a cave in Kaylaka park. Its PDO covers four municipalities.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-plovdiv":{"name":"Plovdiv","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Mavrud, Rubin, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pamid","summary":"Plovdiv, the ancient Philippopolis, is the centre of the Thracian Lowlands; its PDO takes in eight municipalities around the city (Asenovgrad, Kuklen, Perushtitsa, Rodopi, Saedinenie, Brezovo, Parvomai). Mavrud, Rubin, Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot dominate, and the Brestovitsa area is known for Rubin.","producers":["Georgiev & Milkov"],"rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-pomorie":{"name":"Pomorie","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white","red"],"grapes":"Dimyat, Muscat Ottonel, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Pomorie, on a peninsula on the southern Black Sea coast near Burgas, covers four municipalities and is known for Dimyat whites and for grape brandy. The sea moderates temperatures and lengthens the season.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-ruse":{"name":"Ruse","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white","red"],"grapes":"Riesling, Chardonnay, Traminer, Muscat Ottonel, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Ruse, on the Danube opposite Giurgiu in Romania, covers six municipalities. It is known for whites (Riesling, Chardonnay, Traminer) and some reds; the city was the 19th-century gateway for Western wine culture.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-sakar":{"name":"Sakar","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Syrah, Mavrud, Cabernet Franc","summary":"Sakar is a low mountain on the Turkish border near Svilengrad, a historic vineyard area that has become one of Bulgaria's most dynamic since 2000. Its warm, dry slopes on granite and sandy soils grow Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Syrah and Mavrud. Katarzyna and Terra Tangra are the best-known estates.","producers":["Katarzyna","Terra Tangra"],"rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-sandanski":{"name":"Sandanski","cat":"PDO","region":"Struma Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Melnik 55, Shiroka Melnishka Loza, Sandanski Misket, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Sandanski, at the foot of the Pirin in the Struma valley, is one of Bulgaria's warmest wine towns. Its research station bred Melnik 55 in 1963, and the local Sandanski Misket is a rare aromatic white. The PDO covers the Sandanski municipality.","producers":["Damianitza"],"rslug":"struma-valley"},"bg-septemvri":{"name":"Septemvri","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pamid","summary":"Septemvri, at the western end of the Thracian plain where the Maritsa leaves the mountains, has a PDO for its municipality, mainly for reds from Cabernet, Merlot and Pamid. It sits close to the cooler air descending from the Rila and Rhodope mountains, so the wines are fresher than those of the eastern plain.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-shivachevo":{"name":"Shivachevo","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pamid","summary":"Shivachevo, a small town in the Tvarditsa municipality at the foot of the Balkan range, has a small PDO for reds and whites from sheltered slopes. The Balkan range protects the vineyards from northern winds, and the area's old cooperative supplied reds for the export trade.","rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-shumen":{"name":"Shumen","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Traminer, Riesling, Muscat Ottonel, Aligoté","summary":"Shumen, on the plateau of north-east Bulgaria near the medieval capitals Pliska and Preslav, covers Shumen, Novi Pazar and Veliki Preslav municipalities. It is known for whites, especially Chardonnay, Traminer and Riesling, from the large Shumen winery.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-slavyantsi":{"name":"Slavyantsi","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Misket Cherven, Muscat Ottonel, Riesling","summary":"Slavyantsi, a village in the Sungurlare valley, has its own small PDO, also centred on Red Misket and aromatic whites. Its vineyards share the valley's sheltered, cool-night conditions, which preserve the perfume of Misket. Few producers use the name today; most label their wine Sungurlare or Thracian Lowlands PGI.","rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-sliven":{"name":"Sliven","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pamid, Misket, Rkatsiteli","summary":"Sliven, below the Blue Rocks of the eastern Balkan range, covers four municipalities. Its large winery, Vini Sliven, was a key exporter, and the area grows both reds and whites.","rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-stambolovo":{"name":"Stambolovo","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Stambolovo, a village in the eastern Rhodope foothills near Haskovo, has a PDO for its municipality; its old cellar was known in the export era for Merlot. The hot, dry eastern Rhodope foothills ripen Merlot fully, and Stambolovo Merlot was a familiar export label in the 1980s.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-stara-zagora":{"name":"Stara Zagora","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Rubin, Syrah","summary":"The Stara Zagora PDO covers the warm southern slopes of the Sredna Gora around the city of Stara Zagora (Bratya Daskalovi and Opan municipalities). It is red-wine country: Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Rubin and Syrah.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-suhindol":{"name":"Suhindol","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Gamza, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Suhindol, in the hills of the central Danubian plain, is a historic wine village whose cooperative, founded in 1909, is often called Bulgaria's first. In the 1980s its Cabernet Sauvignon and Gamza were among the bestselling Bulgarian wines in Britain. The PDO covers Suhindol and Pavlikeni.","producers":["Lovico Suhindol"],"nerd_note":"Suhindol's cooperative was founded as 'Gamza' in 1909, named after the local grape, decades before the state took over the industry.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-sungurlare":{"name":"Sungurlare","cat":"PDO","region":"Rose Valley","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Misket Cherven, Riesling, Muscat Ottonel, Traminer","summary":"Sungurlare's valley, in the eastern Balkan foothills, is the classic home of Misket Cherven (Red Misket), a pink-skinned aromatic white that gives delicate, floral, slightly spicy wines. The PDO covers Sungurlare, Karnobat and Kotel municipalities.","rslug":"rose-valley"},"bg-svishtov":{"name":"Svishtov","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Gamza, Chardonnay","summary":"Svishtov, on the Danube at Bulgaria's northernmost point, covers the Svishtov and Belene municipalities. Its winery was one of the main suppliers of Cabernet Sauvignon for the export boom, from vineyards on loess bluffs above the river.","rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-targovishte":{"name":"Targovishte","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Muscat Ottonel","summary":"Targovishte, in the eastern Danubian plateau, covers the Targovishte and Loznitsa municipalities; its winery is known for Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc and Riesling. The plateau's cool nights and limestone-rich soils favour crisp whites, as across the north-east.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-varbitsa":{"name":"Varbitsa","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Riesling, Chardonnay, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Varbitsa, in the Shumen province at the northern foot of the eastern Balkan range, has a small single-municipality PDO for whites and reds. The village sits in a sheltered valley where the eastern Balkan range meets the north-eastern plateau, so it combines Black Sea freshness with continental warmth.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-varna":{"name":"Varna","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Dimyat, Riesling, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"Varna's PDO covers the vineyards around Bulgaria's main port (Varna, Aksakovo and Byala municipalities). Coastal whites dominate, from Dimyat, Riesling and Chardonnay. The sea keeps autumns long and mild, so whites ripen slowly and keep their acidity.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-veliki-preslav":{"name":"Veliki Preslav","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Traminer, Riesling, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"Veliki Preslav was the capital of the First Bulgarian Empire in the 10th century. Its PDO covers three municipalities, and its old cellar was famous for Chardonnay and Traminer whites.","rslug":"black-sea"},"bg-vidin":{"name":"Vidin","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Gamza, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pinot Noir, Chardonnay","summary":"Vidin, in Bulgaria's north-west corner, covers Vidin, Novo Selo and Belogradchik municipalities. It is Gamza country, and its estates include Bononia (named after Roman Vidin) and Magura, whose traditional-method sparkling wine ages in a cave decorated with prehistoric paintings near Rabisha.","producers":["Bononia","Magura","Borovitza","Chateau de Val"],"rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-vratsa":{"name":"Vratsa","cat":"PDO","region":"Danubian Plain","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Gamza, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pinot Noir, Chardonnay","summary":"Vratsa covers seven municipalities of the north-west, from the Balkan foothills to the Danube at Oryahovo and Kozloduy. Burgozone (Oryahovo) and Tipchenitza (Mezdra) are leading estates. The stretch along the Danube is hot and dry, while the Iskar gorge near Mezdra is cooler, so the PDO covers quite different conditions.","producers":["Chateau Burgozone","Tipchenitza"],"rslug":"danubian-plain"},"bg-yambol":{"name":"Yambol","cat":"PDO","region":"Thracian Lowlands","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Pamid, Rkatsiteli, Muscat Ottonel","summary":"The Yambol PDO covers the Tundzha valley around Yambol and Elhovo (five municipalities). It is a large, warm, flat area of Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot and whites, once a major exporter.","rslug":"thracian-lowlands"},"bg-yuzhno-chernomorie":{"name":"Yuzhno Chernomorie","cat":"PDO","region":"Black Sea","created":"EU PDO 2007","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Dimyat, Riesling, Muscat Ottonel, Sauvignon Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Yuzhno Chernomorie ('Southern Black Sea Coast') is a broad PDO covering 13 municipalities around Burgas, from Nesebar and Pomorie to Sozopol and Tsarevo. It is used for whites and reds from coastal and inland vineyards.","rslug":"black-sea"}}};
